# Probe scratch space, and any lock a local run writes into this Skill's own
# directory. `.fgc/` is #17's cache and build scratch, and `fgc.lock.json` belongs to
# the *project* being decided, not to the Skill.
.fgc/
fgc.lock.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored: `fgc-evidence/`, which sits beside the lock and holds the
# probe reports the lock cites. It is the durable half of a decision — a record whose
# evidence cannot travel with it keeps reporting `fresh`/`validated` on a machine that
# never received the bytes, and a `runtime-smoke` result in particular may not be
# reproducible on a reviewer's machine at all. `status` reports an unresolvable
# citation as `evidence-missing` for the same reason. Not listed here on purpose, so a
# future edit to this file does not quietly re-ignore it.

# Local decision files an Agent writes while working. The recording contract is
# `references/decision-recording.md`; a working file is not a delivered artifact.
*.decision.json

node_modules/
*.log
